stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Available
    Available --> ReadyPreparation: normal or strong / cooldown clear
    ReadyPreparation --> Swing: 250 ms / 80 ms pose blends
    state Swing {
        [*] --> Windup
        Windup --> Contact: configured hit or projectile release times
        Contact --> Contact: additional authored impacts or burst shots
        Contact --> SwingRecovery: final impact or release elapsed
        SwingRecovery --> [*]: motion and held recovery complete
    }
    Swing --> Swing: valid queued follow-up and step less than N
    Swing --> FailedRecovery: early or late press and step less than N
    Swing --> StoppedCooldown: no follow-up press and step less than N
    Swing --> FinisherReady: step N completed
    FailedRecovery --> Available: 250 ms / stationary and exposed
    StoppedCooldown --> Available: 300 ms / attacks and guard unlock
    FinisherReady --> Available: 350 ms / movement unlocks
    FinisherReady --> Block: eligible frontal melee
    Block --> Available: block animation completes
    note right of Swing
        Normal and strong use the same queue window.
        One accepted follow-up; duplicates cannot replace it.
        Strong cue occurs during existing windup.
        N and contact schedule belong to the weapon profile.
        Final step accepts no further follow-up.
    end note
    note right of StoppedCooldown
        Movement and dodge available at swing completion.
        Attack cooldown is independent of locomotion.
        No earned guard during this cooldown.
    end note
    note right of FinisherReady
        Prototype has guaranteed frontal guard, not random odds.
        Rear attacks and status ticks are not blocked.
        Failed recovery and preparation cannot guard.
    end note
